course: dictionary
lesson: 6244
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word modelling can mean different things, so context tells you which one. In art, «clay modelling» means making shapes from clay or Plasticine. In science, computer modelling means building a simple copy of how something works, so you can predict what will happen.
explain: «Squash a ball of modelling clay and it sinks in a bowl of water.» Here modelling clay is the soft clay you shape with your hands. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "Squash a ball of making-shapes clay" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Modelling can also mean showing others how to do something. When a teacher shows you a sum step by step, she is modelling the skill, and «modelling good manners» means behaving well so others copy you.
fact: Modelling means making a copy or a simple version of something.
fact: Modelling clay is soft clay that you can press and shape with your hands.
fact: A fashion model wears clothes for photos or shows, and «modelling» can mean that job.
fact: In science and maths, a model is a simple set of rules that shows how something works, and modelling uses it to predict things.
fact: British English spells it «modelling» with two Ls, and American English spells it «modeling» with one L.
exercise: «Squash a ball of modelling clay and it sinks in a bowl of water.» What is modelling clay? | A fashion show for clay | A computer game | *Soft clay you shape by hand to make things | A kind of water for washing paint
exercise: Maya's class is doing computer modelling of the weather. What does it mean? | Wearing clothes for a weather photo | *Making a simple computer version that predicts how the weather may change | Drawing pictures of clouds in colour | Writing a letter to the weather station
exercise: Which phrase means showing others how to behave by doing it yourself? | «computer modelling» | *«modelling good manners» | «clay modelling» | «a modelling agency»
test: In a maths lesson, modelling a real problem turns it into what? | A map of the playground | Paint and glue | A song about shapes | *Numbers and equations
test: Which person does the job called modelling when they wear clothes for photos or shows? | *A fashion model | A computer programmer | A maths teacher | A clay sculptor
exam: Teachers say they are «modelling» a skill, which most likely means: | Hiding it from the class | Making it into a clay shape | Testing you on it straight away | *Showing you how to do it first
